## BEFORE — what each failing group shows about main (the production code)
- test_completion_content_rule x9: main has no completion rule (ImportError: completion_content) — null/empty/wrong-shape completions were not distinguished.
- test_openrouter_path_* x4: main returned ok=True for content null / "" and raised/returned ok=True for wrong structure (fake OpenAI-compatible server on 127.0.0.1).
- test_keyless_malformed_completion_fails_fast_without_retrying: main re-sent a structurally wrong 200 until the retry budget ended (most of the 101 s of this run).
- test_external_agent_malformed_outputs x2: main returned ok=True, answer=None for content null; {"choices": {}} gave a raw error text.
- test_cancelled_background_run_ends_the_record_failed / test_unexpected_error_in_a_run_ends_the_record_failed: the record stayed "running".
- test_execute_route_error_does_not_leave_a_running_record: the execute record stayed "running" after the 500.
- test_queue_duplicate_enqueue_is_idempotent_in_fallback: the fallback queued the same id twice.
- test_queue_redis_mode_retry_requeues_with_the_enqueue_priority: fail() called self.zadd (AttributeError) -> never re-queued.
- test_queue_redis_mode_duplicate_enqueue_is_idempotent: second enqueue overwrote the stored task.
- test_storage_malformed_reads_are_no_rows x4: malformed bodies/rows were handed out as rows; get_task returned rows[0] for another id (read3).
- test_malformed_storage_row_is_404_not_500: GET /api/tasks/{id} answered 500 on a row without task_id.
- tests/test_r160_local_integration.py 5/5 pass on main: they pin observed behaviour that R-160 does not change (abort does not cancel, no SSE replay, duplicates = two tasks, error bodies).
